From: Behdad Esfahbod <behdad@behdad.org>
Date: Thu, 22 Jan 2026 18:08:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [gvar] Fix padding size calcs (#5718)

The previous state of is_long_offset() is irrelevant here.

Fixes https://oss-fuzz.com/testcase-detail/5920156651159552
---
 src/hb-ot-var-gvar-table.hh                      |   2 +-
 ...e-minimized-hb-subset-fuzzer-5920156651159552 | Bin 0 -> 1975 bytes
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 test/fuzzing/fonts/clusterfuzz-testcase-minimized-hb-subset-fuzzer-5920156651159552

diff --git a/src/hb-ot-var-gvar-table.hh b/src/hb-ot-var-gvar-table.hh
index d40b37697b8..a22bbca01b2 100644
--- a/src/hb-ot-var-gvar-table.hh
+++ b/src/hb-ot-var-gvar-table.hh
@@ -488,7 +488,7 @@ struct gvar_GVAR
 
     /* This ordering relative to the shared tuples array, which puts the glyphVariationData
        last in the table, is required when HB_SUBSET_FLAGS_IFTB_REQUIREMENTS is set */
-    if (is_long_offset () && long_offset)
+    if (long_offset)
       subset_data_size -= padding_size;
     char *subset_data = c->serializer->allocate_size<char> (subset_data_size, false);
     if (!subset_data) return_trace (false);
diff --git a/test/fuzzing/fonts/clusterfuzz-testcase-minimized-hb-subset-fuzzer-5920156651159552 b/test/fuzzing/fonts/clusterfuzz-testcase-minimized-hb-subset-fuzzer-5920156651159552
